crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# On PA-7100LC this module performs ~90-50% better, less for longer
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# keys, than code generated by gcc 3.2 for PA-RISC 1.1. Latter means
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# that compiler utilized xmpyu instruction to perform 32x32=64-bit
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# toward 4 times 16x16=32-bit multiplications [plus complementary
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# for PA-RISC 1.1, but the "baseline" is far from optimal. The actual
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# improvement coefficient was never collected on PA-7100LC, or any
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# vendor compiler. But to give you a taste, PA-RISC 1.1 code path
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# of ~5x on PA-8600.
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# On PA-RISC 2.0 it has to compete with pa-risc2[W].s, which is
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# to comment in pa-risc2[W].s]. Here comes a catch. Execution core of
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# this implementation is actually 32-bit one, in the sense that it
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# operates on 32-bit values. But pa-risc2[W].s operates on arrays of
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# 64-bit BN_LONGs... How do they interoperate then? No problem. This
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# module picks halves of 64-bit values in reverse order and pretends
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# they were 32-bit BN_LONGs. But can 32-bit core compete with "pure"
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# 64-bit code such as pa-risc2[W].s then? Well, the thing is that
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# 32x32=64-bit multiplication is the best even PA-RISC 2.0 can do,
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# i.e. there is no "wider" multiplication like on most other 64-bit
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# platforms. This means that even being effectively 32-bit, this
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# implementation performs "64-bit" computational task in same amount
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# seem to exhaust memory port capacity. And indeed, dedicated PA-RISC
crypto/bn/asm/parisc-mont.pl:# 2.0 code path provides virtually same performance as pa-risc2[W].s:
