doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:if no sender name can be determined from the B<-cert> or <-subject> options and
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:is typically used when authenticating with pre-shared key (password-based MAC).
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:=item B<-secret> I<arg>
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:Provides the source of a secret value to use with MAC-based message protection.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:This takes precedence over the B<-cert> and B<-key> options.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:The secret is used for creating MAC-based protection of outgoing messages
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:and for validating incoming messages that have MAC-based protection.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:The algorithm used by default is Password-Based Message Authentication Code (PBM)
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:L<openssl-passphrase-options(1)>.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:=item B<-cert> I<filename>|I<uri>
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:Requires the corresponding key to be given with B<-key>.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:while the subject of B<-oldcert> or B<-subjectName> may provide fallback values.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:When performing signature-based message protection,
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:the certificate to be updated if the B<-oldcert> option is not given.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:is included in the extraCerts field in signature-protected request messages.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:=item B<-own_trusted> I<filenames>|I<uris>
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:the client-side CMP signer certificate given with the B<-cert> option
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:B<-verify_hostname>, B<-verify_ip>, and B<-verify_email>
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:=item B<-key> I<filename>|I<uri>
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:the B<-cert> option.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:This will be used for signature-based message protection unless the B<-secret>
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:option indicating MAC-based protection or B<-unprotected_requests> is given.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:It is also used as a fallback for the B<-newkey> option with IR/CR/KUR messages.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:=item B<-keypass> I<arg>
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:Pass phrase source for the private key given with the B<-key> option.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:Also used for B<-cert> and B<-oldcert> in case it is an encrypted PKCS#12 file.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:L<openssl-passphrase-options(1)>.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:=item B<-digest> I<name>
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:and as the one-way function (OWF) in C<MSG_MAC_ALG>.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:proof-of-possession (POPO) signatures.
doc/man1/openssl-cmp.pod.in:To see the list of supported digests, use C<openssl list -digest-commands>.
